to-thierry-coquand-source : List Word
to-thierry-coquand-source = lines-of (cons "# Thierry Coquand"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Professor of computer science at the University of Gothenburg and Chalmers since 1996, earlier at INRIA under Gérard Huet; holder of the Collège de France annual chair in Computer Sciences and Digital Technologies for 2024–2025, lecturing on dependent type theory and the formalization of mathematics; twice an ERC Advanced Grantee (2009, 2022)."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work did that the field still files under a narrower heading"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field records the Calculus of Constructions as the logic behind a proof assistant, and records the assistant, Coq, now Rocq, by its applications. That is the smaller half of what you did with Huet. You made a single calculus in which a program, a proposition, a proof and a mathematical object are one kind of thing, checked by one judgement. The paper names that lineage as its foundation: dependent type theory as developed by Martin-Löf and by your Calculus of Constructions"
  (cons (cite s2-1-p7 "(§2.1)")
  (cons ", in which a proposition is a type when its inhabitants are the evidence under discussion, and a proof is an inhabitant"
  (cons (cite s2-p11 "(§2)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Cubical type theory is the same move made at the level of equality. Voevodsky's univalence said that equivalent types are equal, but as an axiom it carried no computation. Your paper with Cohen, Huber and Mörtberg gave it a constructive interpretation: a path is a term indexed by an interval coordinate, and the path univalence gives an equivalence is built with Glue types, so that transport along it computes the equivalence's forward action"
  (cons (cite s4-p5 "(§4, 4.1–4.2)")
  (cons ". The field tends to present this as one model of homotopy type theory among several. The paper takes its consequence at full size: an identification of structures transports the operations and their laws together"
  (cons (cite s4-p17 "(§4)")
  (cons ", so a change of representation acts on everything built over it, with the evidence moving too"
  (cons (cite s4-1-p11 "(§4.1)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your Collège de France lectures traced this line from Russell's types through Curry–Howard to Voevodsky's homotopical semantics. Hyperactivity takes that line as its foundation."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity is, in your terms"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik describes hyperactivity as a language and a computational model of reality, Wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon; the paper places itself beside Wolfram's program"
  (cons (cite s1-4-p2 "(§1.4)")
  (cons ". Its computational rules follow your CCHM calculus, extended with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ". The displayed path, composition and filling rules are selected computations of CCHM, and the remaining Kan, universe, face and Glue equations are those of the CCHM calculus"
  (cons (cite s3-4-p9 "(§3.4)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The checker is itself a term: it inspects the evaluator's values through a structured observation, checks their types and conversion, and returns its judgement"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2)")
  (cons ". The workflow places its computation of the Brunerie number beside Cubical Agda computing the same definition (the node brunerie-comparison)."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Types and terms are not two species of artifact, one called data and one called code"
  (cons (cite s2-p9 "(§2)")
  (cons ". A codebase holds programs together with their typing derivations, semantics, equivalences, transformations, dependency certificates and proofs; a definition is stored with its typed syntax tree and dependency references, and a name is a view"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". A rendering, a source view, a proof tree or a trace is a chosen observation of the same retained objects"
  (cons (cite s10-9-p6 "(§10.9)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it takes from you, and what that closes"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**What an observation warrants.** For an observation `o : H → O`, a reading `y` determines the fiber of histories compatible with it"
  (cons (cite s1-p8 "(1.1)")
  (cons ", and what the reading warrants about a conclusion `P` is a construction over that whole fiber"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(1.3)")
  (cons ". Refining the observation can shrink the fiber, so a conclusion established over the coarser fiber stays established for the finer one"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1)")
  (cons ". A law on the whole yields a law on what is observed only when it descends through the observation; the paper's two-bit calculation is a reversible whole whose observed coordinate has no autonomous next-state function at all"
  (cons (cite s1-p16 "(§1, a reversible whole with no observed law)")
  (cons ". Part III applies the same construction to words: the meaning of an occurrence is the family of continuations transported from the past occurrences its context selects, determinate exactly when that family is contractible"
  (cons (cite language-derived-from-the-record-source "(Part III, Language derived from the record)")
  (cons ". All of this is your equality doing semantic work: these two readings are the same is a path, a term the checker examines, and what was derived under one reading transports to the other."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Equivalence as the unit of integration.** A bare equivalence of carriers does not preserve a multiplication, an order or a memory model; the structured type includes its operations and laws, and an identification of structures transports both"
  (cons (cite s4-p17 "(§4, 4.6)")
  (cons ". A proved structured equivalence between two representations carries algorithms and their correctness evidence across the change"
  (cons (cite s4-3-p5 "(§4.3)")
  (cons ". This is available because your constructive interpretation made transport compute."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Proofs beside the code they are about.** An old proof does not silently become a proof about an edited object: its dependent type changes and is inhabited again for the new definition"
  (cons (cite s10-11-p6 "(§10.11)")
  (cons ". Retained results are reused exactly when their dependency certificates, which record each lookup and each absence, still validate"
  (cons (cite s10-1-p2 "(§10.1)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Process, not only proposition.** Continuing processes are represented in clocked cubical type theory, with a later modality and clock quantification, so a guarded process with return, delay and response-indexed commands is a term of the same theory as its specification"
  (cons (cite s7-6-p19 "(§7.6)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The paper's conclusion states what follows: a routine, a relation on its behavior, and a rationale for that relation are constructions in one language, not three authorities between which the engineer must translate"
  (cons (cite s11-p3 "(§11)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Credit"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for every piece of your work this system builds on: the Calculus of Constructions, the identification of programs, proofs and objects it established, and cubical type theory with Cohen, Huber and Mörtberg, which is its core. Nothing here is offered as superseding that work. It is that work taken as the foundation of all computing."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The whole is open to you. Read it looking for where your theory does the most: that is where it is."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, the blocks linked above"
  (cons "- Thierry Coquand, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thierry_Coquand"
  (cons "- Collège de France, Computer Sciences and Digital Technologies annual chair 2024–2025, https://www.college-de-france.fr/en/chair/thierry-coquand-computer-sciences-and-digital-technologies-annual-chair"
  (cons "- University of Gothenburg, second ERC Advanced Grant, 2022, https://www.gu.se/nyheter/professor-inom-data-och-informationsteknik-mottar-prestigefyllt-anslag-for-andra-gangen"
  (cons "- Cohen, Coquand, Huber, Mörtberg, Cubical Type Theory: a constructive interpretation of the univalence axiom, https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.02108"
  (cons "- Chalmers research profile, https://research.chalmers.se/en/person/coquand"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
